\section{Automated Error Handling \& Adaptive Recovery Loop}

\subsection{Recovery Mechanisms}

\paragraph{1. CFL Violation Interception}
If
\[
\frac{v_{\max}\Delta t}{\Delta x}
+
2\frac{D_{\max}\Delta t}{(\Delta x)^2}
> 1,
\]
the timestep is compressed:
\[
\Delta t \leftarrow \frac{\Delta t}{2}.
\]

\paragraph{2. Matrix Re-conditioning}
Stiff ODE subsystems (enzymatic kinetics, CTSHA transitions) are switched from explicit Runge--Kutta to implicit BDF solvers.

\paragraph{3. Energy Damping Injection}
The Hamiltonian dissipation coefficient is increased:
\[
\gamma \leftarrow \gamma_{\mathrm{new}} > \gamma_{\mathrm{old}},
\]
to bleed excess kinetic energy and return the trajectory to the Lyapunov basin of attraction.